{"key":"enterprise/T1098.004","id":"T1098.004","name":"SSH Authorized Keys","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1098","tactics":["persistence","privilege-escalation"],"platforms":["ESXi","IaaS","Linux","macOS","Network Devices"],"environments":["cloud","cloud-hosted-endpoint","network-infrastructure","onprem","virtualization"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may modify the SSH authorized_keys file to maintain persistence on a victim host. Linux distributions, macOS, and ESXi hypervisors commonly use key-based authentication to secure the authentication process of SSH sessions for remote management. The authorized_keys file in SSH specifies the SSH keys that can be used for logging into the user account for which the file is configured. This file is usually found in the user's home…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1098/004","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--6b57dc31-b814-4a03-8706-28bc20d739c4","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.640Z","source_object_version":"1.4","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0064","name":"Command Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0064","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--685f917a-e95e-4ba0-ade1-c7d354dae6e0","page":"telemetry/DC0064/"},{"id":"DC0061","name":"File Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0061","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--84572de3-9583-4c73-aabd-06ea88123dd8","page":"telemetry/DC0061/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0126","name":"Detection Strategy for SSH Key Injection in Authorized Keys","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0126","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--cf33849d-67f4-418e-9a41-6a6c082e576a","relationship_id":"relationship--ace534ca-793